r":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T07:41:09-07:00","id":975509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975370-how-to-improve-the-dread-horror-rules#post975370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my favorite parts of the CofD is the Dread Horror monster maker rules. I have played with it some, and really like it. Still, it feels like something's missing. I had been hoping they might make a blue supplement book to expand it someday. How would you improve it? Does anyone have any house rules they use that make it even better?</div> </div> </div> </div> Hunter will most likely adding dread powers and stuff to the horror rules, as I believe Hunter was the inspiration for the Horrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T10:16:28-07:00","id":975573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975370-how-to-improve-the-dread-horror-rules?p=975509#post975509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hunter will most likely adding dread powers and stuff to the horror rules, as I believe Hunter was the inspiration for the Horrors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was already interested in Hunter, this is good news.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T10:17:54-07:00","id":975574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975370-how-to-improve-the-dread-horror-rules?p=975461#post975461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from increasing the number of Dread Powers tied to a Horror's Potency? None, so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of innovations. Maybe a expanded chapter in coming up with the backgrounds for unique monsters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T10:24:54-07:00","id":975577,"title":"","content":"Some things I would like to see in a supplement book about Dread Horrors.<br /> <br /> 1. A chapter that guides you on coming up with the backstory of a horror, and secrets for the players to uncover. A little like city creation from Damnation city, but aimed at creating backgrounds for monster.<br /> <br /> 2. A chapter on creating Dread Locations, with guides and mechanics for the players to interact with.<br /> <br /> 3. Expanded rules and guidelines for playing Dread Horrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T10:37:17-07:00","id":975584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975370-how-to-improve-the-dread-horror-rules?p=975573#post975573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was already interested in Hunter, this is good news.</div> </div> </div> </div> This isn't a certainty, but the ideas, such as Dread powers, have their origin in Hunter: The Vigil 1e, so I'd be shocked if they weren't in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T13:27:53-07:00","id":975679,"title":"","content":"What I would have liked, and this won't be possible until a 3e, is for each splat to contain Horror rules for making the splat itself. Like Vampire has Dread Powers for the Strix, but none for a Vampire. What I really like are the brief nightmare rules, that's imo much better than fully statting characters. In theory, you can also use the powers from Mortal Remains, I haven't tried them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T13:43:29-07:00","id":975685,"title":"","content":"xenoterracide, what's 3rd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T13:56:19-07:00","id":975688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975370-how-to-improve-the-dread-horror-rules?p=975685#post975685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">xenoterracide, what's 3rd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>theoretically a product after they're done making 2e about 10 years from now","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T14:04:27-07:00","id":975691,"title":"","content":"Xenoterracide, you're killing me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T23:21:05-07:00","id":975849,"title":"","content":"I have worked quite a bit with the Horror Rules since the release of the Chronicles of Darkness. As they are, the rules work pretty fine, but I have made some observations and adjustments.<br /> <br /> The Brief Nightmare rules are excellent for many types of Monster of the Week. You don't need a ton of detail if the intent of the creature is to menace the players for an evening or two.<br /> <br /> The standard rules are best when you need a more detailed creature that is more of a character in its own right, or you simply prefer to go into more detail when creating creatures and antagonists.<br /> <br /> With the Standard Rule, I frequently reduce the number of skills points a creature gets with their potency in order to add an additional dread power or merit dots. This is often best if the creature is animalistic enough to to have a deep selection of skills.<br /> <br /> Depending on the creature concept, I often add an additional point of armor or a set of natural weapons without tying it to a dread power. This is best for standard attacks and defenses - anything more exotics and specialized should definitely be a Dread Power.<br /> <br /> Beyond the core set of Dread Powers, I will import Dread Powers or equivalent from other CofD books. I find some of the material in Beast (Merits and Atavisms), Demon (Cryptids),and Werewolf (Claimed and Hosts) to be suitable and similarly balanced.<br /> Even the more dots-per-level -style Dread Powers presented on Hunter, Promethean or Vampire can be adapted without alot of effort (I normally treat these effects as having 2-3dots when adapting to the Horror-Style Dread Powers)<br /> <br /> I have a link to the Horrors I have created in my sig (shameless plug!). I hope this helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T23:36:50-07:00","id":975855,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Reighnhell;n975849]I have worked quite a bit with the Horror Rules since the release of the Chronicles of Darkness. As they are, the rules work pretty fine, but I have made some observations and adjustments.<br /> <br /> The Brief Nightmare rules are excellent for many types of Monster of the Week. You don't need a ton of detail if the intent of the creature is to menace the players for an evening or two.<br /> <br /> The standard rules are best when you need a more detailed creature that is more of a character in its own right, or you simply prefer to go into more detail when creating creatures and antagonists.<br /> <br /> With the Standard Rule, I frequently reduce the number of skills points a creature gets with their potency in order to add an additional dread power or merit dots. This is often best if the creature is animalistic enough to to have a deep selection of skills.<br /> <br /> Depending on the creature concept, I often add an additional point of armor or a set of natural weapons without tying it to a dread power. This is best for standard attacks and defenses - anything more exotics and specialized should definitely be a Dread Power.<br /> <br /> Beyond the core set of Dread Powers, I will import Dread Powers or equivalent from other CofD books. I find some of the material in Beast (Merits and Atavisms), Demon (Cryptids),and Werewolf (Claimed and Hosts) to be suitable and similarly balanced.<br /> Even the more dots-per-level -style Dread Powers presented on Hunter, Promethean or Vampire can be adapted without alot of effort (I normally treat these effects as having 2-3dots when adapting to the Horror-Style Dread Powers)<br /> <br /> I have a link to the Horrors I have created in my sig (shameless plug!). I hope this helps.[/QU<br /> It does help. I'll go look at your dread powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}